# Go Backend Rules

## Layout

```
backend/
├── cmd/server/main.go
├── internal/
│   ├── handler/       # HTTP handlers — thin, delegate to service
│   ├── service/       # Business logic
│   ├── repository/    # Database access (pgx)
│   └── model/         # Domain types
└── pkg/               # Shared utilities (only if truly reusable)
```

## Standards

- Go 1.22+, stdlib first
- PostgreSQL via `pgx` — no ORM
- Wrap errors with context: `fmt.Errorf("create project: %w", err)`
- Never swallow errors silently
- Table-driven tests in co-located `*_test.go` files

## Handlers

- Validate input at the handler layer
- Return consistent JSON error responses
- Do not access the database directly from handlers

## Secrets

- Never return decrypted secret values in list endpoints
- Redact secret values in structured logs
- Encrypt at rest (Phase 2)
